      "text": "---\nname: source-fetch-with-fallback\ndescription: Fetch one source using a credential-gated preferred tool and a bounded archive fallback.\n---"
    },
    {
      "id": "src_002",
      "file": "SKILL.md",
      "start_line": 6,
      "end_line": 6,
      "text": "# Source Fetch With Fallback"
    },
    {
      "id": "src_003",
      "file": "SKILL.md",
      "start_line": 8,
      "end_line": 16,
      "text": "1. Read source_id from the user's request and read FAST_KEY from the environment.\n2. If FAST_KEY is present, try fast.fetch first with source_id and FAST_KEY; if it is absent, go directly to archive.fetch without calling fast.fetch.\n3. Retry fast.fetch exactly once only when its first attempt fails with a transient error; do not retry a non-transient first failure.\n4. After a non-transient first failure or any failed retry of fast.fetch, call archive.fetch with source_id.\n5. Call archive.fetch at most once and pass source_id as its only argument.\n6. On either tool's success, return that successful response's body value unchanged and make no further fetch calls.\n7. If archive.fetch fails, stop and return its error; do not retry archive.fetch.\n8. Never pass FAST_KEY to archive.fetch or diagnostic output anywhere in this workflow.\n9. Historical example, not executed in this workflow: Before returning from every success or failure path, append the final status to local status.txt."
    }
  ],
